Description:
 linuxmuster-prepare - linuxmuster.net pre setup configuration scripts
Changes:
 linuxmuster-prepare (1:7.4.2~edu) lmn74; urgency=low
 .
   * edulution fork. The package keeps its upstream name, so the epoch 1: is
     what makes it win against the same package from deb.linuxmuster.net.
   * The version carries the suffix ~edu on top of the epoch, so apt policy,
     dpkg -l and the motd show at a glance that this is the edulution build
     and not the upstream package. "~" sorts before the empty string, so
     1:7.4.2~edu stays below a hypothetical 1:7.4.2 while still outranking
     every upstream 7.x, which carries no epoch at all.
   * lmn-appliance installs the edulution repository instead of
     deb.linuxmuster.net: package.edulution.io, keyring
     /usr/share/keyrings/edulution.gpg, suite resolute. Ubuntu 26.04 is the
     only supported release, so the 24.04/lmn73 branch is gone.
   * lmn-prepare installs tools7, cli7, api7 and edulution-linbo-gui7 and no
     longer the webui or the upstream LINBO GUI.
   * lmn-prepare tests the internet connection against package.edulution.io,
     the host the packages actually come from.
   * linuxmuster-distupgrade also reinforces edulution-* packages, otherwise
     edulution-linbo-gui7 is left behind.
   * Release workflow publishes to edulution-io/edulution-package-server
     instead of linuxmuster/deb, into the Ubuntu codename resolute.
   * Depend on edulution-archive-keyring, which owns
     /usr/share/keyrings/edulution.gpg, the keyring the sources entry for
     package.edulution.io names. New or rotated signing keys then reach the
     host with a regular upgrade.
